# PLAN_CONSOLIDATION item 7 (Dave 2026-10-10): every Zernike-carrying surface defaults
# to ZernType= ANSI whatever its element type.  Three twins (ZGD_test_files/
# tst_zerndef_*.in): a ZrnGrData NS primary with ZernCoef mode 9 = 2e-7 m and NO type /
# ANSI / Fringe.  The undeclared twin must trace EXACTLY as the ANSI one (RMS and P-V
# printed identically); Fringe must differ.  Pre-change the undeclared twin traced as
# the bare conic (ZernTypeL 0: its coefficients never reached the trace) -- red.
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_zerndef_none.in
opd 6
/null
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_zerndef_ansi.in
opd 6
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_zerndef_fringe.in
opd 6
# EXPECT: tst_zerndef_none\.in[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+(\S+)[^\n]*\n\s*P-V OPD error is\s+(\S+)[\s\S]*?tst_zerndef_ansi\.in[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+\1\s[^\n]*\n\s*P-V OPD error is\s+\2\s
# EXPECT: tst_zerndef_none\.in[\s\S]*?Default used for ZernType\(\s+2\)[\s\S]*?tst_zerndef_ansi\.in
# EXPECT-NOT: tst_zerndef_ansi\.in[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+(\S+)[\s\S]*?tst_zerndef_fringe\.in[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+\1\s
